### reco health
GET http://localhost:8086/actuator/health
X-Request-Id: manual-reco-health

### reco liveness
GET http://localhost:8086/actuator/health/liveness

### reco prometheus
GET http://localhost:8086/actuator/prometheus

### ---- P14 (ADR-0020): the recommendation and its explanation. Every route needs a USER token: sign in via
### identity.http (POST /v1/auth/login) and paste the accessToken below. There is nothing to POST - the recompute
### is event-driven (the sweeper) or happens inside the read when the inputs have moved.
@token = PASTE_AN_ACCESS_TOKEN
@cardProductId = PASTE_A_CARD_PRODUCT_ID

### recommendations: the ranking, plus the cards that did not clear the threshold.
### `recommended` is sorted by the blended score (60 % rupees saved, 40 % expense fit). A card you already hold is
### marked `held: true` rather than dropped, because "you already have the best card for this" is worth seeing.
### `fresh` is always true: a read recomputes when the stored result's state hash no longer matches the inputs.
GET http://localhost:8086/v1/recommendations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Request-Id: manual-reco-list

### recommendations: score only these products - for ranking a search result rather than the whole catalog.
### A subset is never cached: it is a different question from "what should I get".
GET http://localhost:8086/v1/recommendations?cardProductIds={{cardProductId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Request-Id: manual-reco-subset

### explain: the arithmetic behind one card, not a number.
### `lines` is one row per category root: the rule that earned, the share of the root it was credited with
### (Rules.share, A-81), the spend considered, what it earned, and whether a cap bound it. `fee` carries the annual
### fee, the waiver threshold and the probability the account's spend clears it. `milestone` is counted only when
### the spend reaches it. savings = rewards - expected fee + milestone.
GET http://localhost:8086/v1/recommendations/explain/{{cardProductId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Request-Id: manual-reco-explain

### explain: a product the catalog projection does not have as published -> 404 CARD_NOT_IN_CATALOG
GET http://localhost:8086/v1/recommendations/explain/00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Request-Id: manual-reco-explain-404

### an admin-console token cannot act as a user -> 403 USER_TOKEN_REQUIRED
GET http://localhost:8086/v1/recommendations
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_AN_ADMIN_TOKEN
X-Request-Id: manual-reco-admin-refused

### P15 · the wallet: the best one, two and three card wallets, and what each further card adds
GET http://localhost:8086/v1/recommendations/wallet
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Request-Id: manual-reco-wallet

### the wallet, capped at a single card
GET http://localhost:8086/v1/recommendations/wallet?size=1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Request-Id: manual-reco-wallet-one

### a wallet bigger than three cards -> 400
GET http://localhost:8086/v1/recommendations/wallet?size=9
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Request-Id: manual-reco-wallet-too-big

### P15 · best card for one purchase: Rs 2,500 of dining, over the cards the account holds
GET http://localhost:8086/v1/recommendations/best-card?amountPaise=250000&category=food.dining
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Request-Id: manual-reco-bestcard

### the same purchase at a known merchant: a merchant rule beats the category rule
GET http://localhost:8086/v1/recommendations/best-card?amountPaise=250000&category=food.dining&merchantId=PASTE_A_MERCHANT_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Request-Id: manual-reco-bestcard-merchant

### no amount -> 400 AMOUNT_REQUIRED
GET http://localhost:8086/v1/recommendations/best-card?amountPaise=0&category=food.dining
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Request-Id: manual-reco-bestcard-no-amount

### neither merchant nor category -> 400 MERCHANT_OR_CATEGORY_REQUIRED
GET http://localhost:8086/v1/recommendations/best-card?amountPaise=250000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Request-Id: manual-reco-bestcard-no-scope

### P15 · mint a one-time stream ticket (60 s), because EventSource cannot send an Authorization header
POST http://localhost:8086/v1/recommendations/stream-ticket
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Request-Id: manual-reco-ticket

### open the stream with it. No token: the ticket is the credential. Paste the ticket from the call above.
GET http://localhost:8086/v1/recommendations/stream?ticket=PASTE_THE_TICKET
Accept: text/event-stream
X-Request-Id: manual-reco-stream

### the same ticket a second time -> 401 STREAM_TICKET_INVALID (single use)
GET http://localhost:8086/v1/recommendations/stream?ticket=PASTE_THE_SAME_TICKET
Accept: text/event-stream
X-Request-Id: manual-reco-stream-replay
